text='''# Empirical revision protocol\n\nHistorical analyses execute first. The protected outer partitions are unchanged. Three grouped inner folds and two development seeds select six neural configurations. Ten specified final seeds use a predeclared grouped validation holdout; every trajectory has up to 500 epochs, minimum 50 and patience 50, with best checkpoint selected from all epochs. No APP/S7 labels select configurations or stopping epochs. Their earlier examination makes this retrospective follow-up.\n\nThe four controlled graph/no-message arms share feature masking and context handling. Only relation weight sharing is crossed with neighbor-state dependence. Support means positive training occurrence, not adequate sample size.\n\nPair activity selection uses endpoint activity error; pair-supervised selection uses measured pair error. The positive loss-weight grid is 0.1, 1, 10 in training-SD-normalized loss units. Every endpoint and its sequence component stays in one fold. B3 remains measurement-dependent; no synthetic labels.\n\nThe deterministic guide/pairwise ridge methods fit once per selected partition. Stochastic tree and neural methods fit all ten seeds. Official published method reproduction is a separate bounded acquisition/dependency stage with up to 100 reserved fits; exact feasibility and any protocol differences must be frozen before its outcomes.\n\nThe machine-readable protocol and full fit matrix are authoritative. Resources remain two CPU threads and 30% of GPU0 memory. Expected 4–18 GPU-region hours and 9–20 GB new storage; hard campaign wall bound 48h. No historical cost ledger is consumed. Failed finite/unstable outcomes remain; only genuinely nonfinite fits get a flagged training-mean fallback.\n\nStage graph: legacy analysis → protocol → scientific checks → activity and pair fits → evaluation → figures → paper → delivery. Source checks run independently and join the paper stage.\n'''
